eners for food products, pharmaceuticals, cosmetics, cigarette filters, high-tenacity rayon tire cords and industrial hoses, food casings, paints, lacquers, munitions, and explosives; and biomaterials, including biofuels, lignosulfonates, prebiotics, tall oil soap, and HCE and turpentine. It also offers commodity products, such as commodity viscose used in woven applications, including rayon textiles for clothing and other fabrics, as well as in non-woven applications comprising baby wipes, cosmetic and personal wipes, industrial wipes, and mattress ticking; and absorbent materials consisting of fluff that are used as an absorbent medium in disposable baby diapers, feminine hygiene products, incontinence pads, convalescent bed pads, industrial towels and wipes, and non-woven fabrics. In addition, the company provides paperboards for packaging, printing documents, brochures, promotional materials, paperback books and catalog covers, file folders, freezer, tags, and lottery tickets; and high-yield pulps to produce hardwood aspen, maple, and birch species for paperboard, packaging, printing and writing papers, and various other paper products. Rayonier Advanced Materials Inc. was founded in 1926 and is headquartered in Jacksonville, Florida.","ceo_bio":"Mr. Daniel M. Krawczyk | CEO, President & Director | Age 55","culture_narrative":"Employs approximately 2K people. Revenue per employee of $631K ranks in the below the sector median among Basic Materials peers. Stock-based compensation of $2K per employee reflects an ownership culture. Governance score flags low compensation governance risk (1/10).","financial_summary":["Rayonier Advanced Materials Inc is a small-cap basic materials business with a $399M market cap on $1.5B of annual revenue.","The top line has compounded at -5% over the past three years and +5% annually across the full decade, and a shrinking top line is the hardest headwind any business can overcome.","Returns on capital run at 0% against a 12% cost of capital, which means the business is destroying value with every dollar it reinvests, and 8% gross margins are typical of commodity economics where competitors can replicate the product cheaply.","The company is burning through $92M of cash, and without positive owner earnings any valuation rests on hope rather than evidence.","Accruals are elevated at -25.3% of assets, and Sloan showed firms building earnings through accruals rather than cash systematically underperform.","On the balance sheet, debt is heavy at 5.1\u00d7 net debt/EBITDA, and leverage like that is what turns a bad year into a permanent loss, and thin 0.0\u00d7 interest coverage leaves no room for a bad year.","Shareholder yield is only 0.0%, a thin return of capital, and insiders hold 5.0% of the shares, and profit capture is only 0.0\u00d7 the fair share, suggesting no structural edge inside its industry."],"sector_headwinds":[{"text":"Altman Z in the distress zone (1.1) \u2014 the kind of balance-sheet risk that can make a loss permanent","sev":"red","cat":"quality"},{"text":"Low reinvestment-driven growth suggests the compounding engine has stalled","sev":"amber","cat":"growth"},{"text":"Operating margins 9% below sector median \u2014 a cost disadvantage the moat cannot hide","sev":"amber","cat":"moat"},{"text":"Fragmented industry with below-average profit capture \u2014 no moat to protect margins","sev":"amber","cat":"moat"},{"text":"Volatile returns on capital suggest the moat is narrower than a snapshot ROIC implies","sev":"amber","cat":"moat"},{"text":"Piotroski score 4/9 \u2014 below the median for a healthy business","sev":"amber","cat":"quality"},{"text":"Above-average short interest at 7.1% of float","sev":"amber","cat":"sentiment"},{"text":"Gross margin trails most Basic Materials peers \u2014 competitors appear to have the pricing hand","sev":"amber","cat":"moat"},{"text":"Carries more leverage than most Basic Materials peers \u2014 a smaller cushion for the inevitable bad year","sev":"amber","cat":"balance_sheet"},{"text":"Trade policy and tariff whiplash \u2014 materials producers are first-order casualties of protectionist swings, and margin gets squeezed from both input and output pricing.","sev":"amber","cat":"thesis_risk"}],"sector_tailwinds":["Shares offer a 23% margin of safety against estimated fair value","Trading near the bottom of its 52-week range \u2014 the market is offering a discount"],"news_headlines":[{"title":"Rayonier Advanced Materials Inc (RYAM) Q3 2026 Earnings Call Highlights: HPC Segment Shines ...","source":"finance.yahoo.com","link":"https://finance.yahoo.com/markets/stocks/articles/rayonier-advanced-materials-inc-ryam-011153395.html","date":"2026-11-07","timestamp":1794013913.0,"origin":"tiingo","sentiment":0.318,"tier":0,"scope":"company","tags":["earnings"]},{"title":"Rayonier Reports Q3 2026 Revenue of $565.6M and Narrowed Nine-Month Net Income","source":"kalkinemedia.com","link":"https://kalkinemedia.com/us/news/announcements/rayonier-reports-q3-2026-revenue-of-5656m-and-narrowed-nine-month-net-income","date":"2026-11-06","timestamp":1794003691.0,"origin":"tiingo","sentiment":0.0,"tier":2,"scope":"company","tags":["earnings"]},{"title":"Rayonier Inc (RYN) (Q3 2026) Earnings Call Highlights: Record Adjusted EBITDA, Aggressive ...","source":"finance.yahoo.com","link":"https://finance.yahoo.com/markets/stocks/articles/rayonier-inc-ryn-q3-2026-090923885.html","date":"2026-11-06","timestamp":1793956163.0,"origin":"tiingo","sentiment":0.273,"tier":2,"scope":"company","tags":["earnings"]},{"title":"Rayonier (RYN) Stock May Be 42% Undervalued On Cash Flow","source":"finance.yahoo.com","link":"https://finance.yahoo.com/markets/stocks/articles/rayonier-ryn-stock-may-42-051602874.html","date":"2026-11-06","timestamp":1793942162.0,"origin":"tiingo","sentiment":0.872,"tier":2,"scope":"company","tags":[]},{"title":"Rayonier (RYN) Q3 2026 Earnings Call Transcript","source":"aol.com","link":"https://www.aol.com/articles/rayonie